__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.coverage

# dogfood loop scratch (the kit runs its own SDLC locally; not part of the plugin)
.sdlc/

# Python build/venv trees (insight/ becomes pip-installable in E0.S2). /build/ and /dist/ are
# anchored to the repo root: unanchored they would match at any depth and untrack a real module
# like insight/metrics/dist/. .venv, venv and *.egg-info ARE unanchored on purpose and therefore
# do still reserve those three names under insight/ — accepted, because none of them is a module
# name anyone would choose, unlike build/ and dist/.
# NOTE: tests/test_licence_boundary.py does NOT read these rules. Its skip is its own
# (pyvenv.cfg + bin|Scripts, __pycache__, *.egg-info), so guard coverage never depends on
# ignore configuration, local or global.
.venv/
venv/
/build/
/dist/
*.egg-info/

# node_modules (insight/web/, E17.S1) — unanchored like .venv/venv above: not a name any real module
# would choose, and scripts/verify_web.py installs into it fresh in every worktree (issue #295).
node_modules/

# insight/ is ALSO its own pip project root (package-dir = {"insight" = "."}), so a plain
# `pip install insight/` — which verify.command (E0.S3, issue #96) now runs on every goal —
# does setuptools' normal in-place `bdist_wheel`, scratch-building into insight/build/ exactly
# the way it would at the repo root. /build/ and /dist/ above do NOT catch this: they are
# anchored to the repo root only (on purpose, see above), so without these two lines
# insight/build/ would sit untracked-but-not-ignored after every local verify run — one
# `git add -A` away from being committed. Anchored the same specific way, one level deeper, for
# the same reason: unanchored would also swallow a real insight/metrics/dist/ or similar.
/insight/build/
/insight/dist/
